Algorithm: Doubly Linked List for Managing Layers
1.Start.
2.Create an empty doubly linked list by setting HEAD = NULL and TAIL = NULL.
3.Display the menu:
•Insert layer at the top.
•Insert layer at the bottom.
•Delete inactive layer.
•Reorder layer.
•Display layers.
•Exit.
4.Read the user's choice.
5.If the user selects Insert Layer at Top:
•Create a new layer node.
•Set its next pointer to HEAD.
•Set its prev pointer to NULL.
•Update HEAD and, if required, TAIL.
•If the user selects Insert Layer at Bottom:
•Create a new layer node.
•Set its prev pointer to TAIL.
•Set its next pointer to NULL.
•Update TAIL and, if required, HEAD.
7.If the user selects Delete Inactive Layer: 
•Search for the inactive layer.
•Adjust the prev and next pointers of the neighbouring nodes.
•Update HEAD and TAIL if required.
•Delete the selected node.
8.If the user selects Reorder Layer:
•Find the required layer.
•Remove it from its current position.
•Insert it at the new position by updating the pointers.
9.If the user selects Display Layers:
•Traverse the list from HEAD to TAIL.
•Display all layers sequentially to represent the final canvas.
10.Repeat steps 3–9 until the user selects Exit.
11.Stop.
